        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0601" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Runyon to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 420]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch, No. 355, of
                    September 2 last, reporting my action in regard to the indorsement by a German
                    official on the passport issued by the State Department to Mr. Jacob Malin
                    Weiler, and held by him, of a statement that the latter had been expelled from
                    Prussian territory, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a note, with
                    translation of the same, received by me to-day from the Imperial foreign office
                    on the subject, from which it appears that the act complained of was without any
                    authority and is wholly disapproved, and that steps have been taken to prevent
                    such action in the future.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore Runyon</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d525-a1.xml" xpointer="d525-a1"/>
